1. The preset is fitted on ``t0 -> t1`` with one step per year;
2. ``validate``: the model simulates the observed period from ``t0``
   and its last map is compared with ``t1`` (`agreement()`);
3. ``until``: the model projects from ``t1``, a step per year.

A coarser, faster summary than [`mspa()`][terraflux.mspa]:

- ``2``: contiguous habitat (core, edge, perforation) and small linear
  features (margin);
- ``3``: core, edge (with perforation) and margin;
- ``5``: core, edge, perforation and margin;
- ``6``: core, edge, perforation, margin and islet.

Only cells off the edge whose 8 neighbours all have a value can be peaks;
heights are compared with 0, so remove the mean or trend first
(`remove_plane()`).

